            "text": "In *Call of Duty*, eliminating opponents comes down to the core combat mechanics, which depend slightly on your platform (PC or console):\n\n### Basic Controls\n* **Aiming (ADS):** Hold **Right-Click** (PC) or **L2 / LT** (PlayStation / Xbox) to Aim Down Sights for increased accuracy.\n* **Shooting:** Press **Left-Click** (PC) or **R2 / RT** (PlayStation / Xbox) to fire your weapon.\n* **Hipfire:** Firing without aiming down sights is faster and useful in very close quarters, but much less accurate at range.\n* **Melee:** Press **V** or click the **Right Thumbstick (R3)** when standing directly next to an enemy to hit them with a melee strike or a knife. A melee hit from behind is usually an instant kill or triggers a \"Finishing Move\" if you hold the button.\n* **Lethal Equipment:** Press **G** or **R1 / RB** to throw lethal equipment like Frag Grenades, Semtex, or Throwing Knives.\n\n---\n\n### Tips for Winning Gunfights\n1. **Aim for the Head and Upper Chest:** Headshots deal significantly more damage than body or limb shots, reducing the time to kill (TTK).\n2. **Control Recoil:** Pull your mouse or right thumbstick slightly downward while firing automatic weapons to counteract the upward kick.\n3. **Use Cover:** Avoid running in the open. Move between objects, corners, and head-glitches (positions where only your head is visible to the enemy).\n4. **Pre-Aiming:** Aim down your sights before turning corners where you anticipate an enemy might be waiting.\n5. **Use the Minimap:** Look for red dots on the radar, which indicate unsuppressed enemy gunfire, to track down targets.\n6. **Customize Weapons (Gunsmith):** Modify your guns with attachments to reduce recoil, increase bullet velocity, and improve aim-down-sights (ADS) speed.",
